# Supr-context MCP write (na-design-system @ Petrov.local)

PostgreSQL via `supr-context` is the source of truth. Chat memory never overrides it.

## Endpoint / identity

- Prefer project MCP **`supr-context-remote`** → `https://context.supriyadies.work/mcp`
- This repo’s ApiClient instance: **`cursor-na-design-system`** (principal `cursor`)
- Local secret file (gitignored, mode 0600): `.supr-context-credentials.json`
- Local MCP config (gitignored): `.cursor/mcp.json` — generate from credentials; see `.cursor/mcp.json.example`
- Never commit API keys, credentials JSON, `.env*`, or live `.cursor/mcp.json`
- Instance identity comes from the Bearer key. Never send `apiClientId`, `clientInstanceId`, or internal `sess_…`

## When to write

Only when the user explicitly wants something durable, e.g. “Remember…”, “Record this decision…”, “Update our position…”, or clear approval after you propose a write.

## When not to write

Casual chat, brainstorming, speculative ideas, temporary notes, invented facts, or overwriting truth without supersession.

## Tool map

| Intent | Tool |
|--------|------|
| Fact / preference / summary / observation | `context_remember` |
| Canonical decision | `context_record_decision` |
| Point-in-time event | `context_record_event` |

Read first with `context_resolve` (broad) or `context_search` / `context_get` (targeted).

## Supersession

1. Resolve or get the current `recordId`
2. Write with `supersedes: <recordId>` — no parallel conflicting truths

## Provenance / actor

- `provider: cursor`, `surface: cursor-ide`
- Truth actor usually `actorSlug: heru` (HUMAN who owns the statement)
- Never expose API keys in replies
